====================================================================================================
I -- IS ANY k^4 GENERATED?  (this is the whole question -- Gen-1 died of k^4)
====================================================================================================
  [DERIVED] STRUCTURAL, from E5: gamma^TT enters T_ij ONLY through -delta Gamma^k_ij a^(0)_k, which is FIRST order in d(gamma).  Y_a is quadratic in T.  Hence the direct TT-TT content of Y_a is EXACTLY k^2 and can never be k^4.  Gen-1's Y_R used delta Rbar_ij ~ d^2 gamma, hence k^4.  This is a statement about the operator, not about a limit.
  [DERIVED] INDIRECT, from D2 + G5 + H4: the only route to k^4 was Y_a -> (d_i d_j delta N)^2 with delta N = kappa gamma.  Two independent facts close it.  (a) The k^3 piece of the lapse source vanishes identically (D2).  (b) The lapse kernel is O(eps A k^4/abar^2) (G5).  Hence kappa = O(a abar^2/(eps A k^3)) and the fed-back term is O(a^2 abar^2/(eps A k^2)) -- it DECREASES with k (H4).  No k^4, and not even a k^2.
  [DERIVED] The one regime where the fed-back term is NOT decreasing is k below the kernel zero (section K), where it tends to a constant -- i.e. a mass term.  Still no k^4 anywhere.

====================================================================================================
J -- NUMBERS: c_T, GW170817, and the bound on eps
====================================================================================================
  a0 = 9.3619e-11 m/s^2 (INPUT)   abar = a0/c^2 = 1.0417e-27 1/m   c^2/a0 = 9.6001e+26 m

  c_T^2/c^2 = G_T/K_T = 1 + 2 eps A(X_0) X_0        [K_T = 1 exactly]
  |c_T/c - 1| = |sqrt(1 + 2 eps A X_0) - 1| ~= eps A(X_0) X_0 = eps X_0^3/(1+X_0)^4
  <-- NOTE: ya_tensor_exact_2026.py compared 2 eps A X_0 (which is delta c_T^2/c^2)
      directly against the |c_T/c - 1| bound.  The correct quantity is HALF that.
  [ok ] J1  max over X_0 of  A(X_0) X_0 = X_0^3/(1+X_0)^4  is at X_0 = 3, value 27/256 = 0.105469
         so the bound is conservative over the whole range of galactic/solar accelerations
  |c_T/c-1| < 1e-15    (conventional GW170817 quote)         =>  eps < 9.481e-15
  c_T/c-1  < +7e-16    (superluminal side, the relevant one for eps>0) =>  eps < 6.637e-15

  eps the Solar-System window wants:  ~1.1e-24
  worst-case |c_T/c - 1| there:       1.160e-25
  [ok ] J2  *** GEN-2 PASSES GW170817 WITH THE CONSTRAINTS SOLVED ***
         margin 6.03e+09x;  Gen-1 FAILED the same test by ~29 orders.  The k^2-vs-k^4 distinction is what does it, and it survives constraint elimination unchanged.

  sign: eps > 0 gives c_T > c (superluminal) since A X_0 > 0; eps < 0 gives c_T < c.
  GW170817 headroom on |eps|:  6.03e+09x the Solar-System value (~10 orders)

